  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\n\nHigh pressure building off the Four Corners region will continue \nwarm and dry conditions Wednesday through late week. A mostly flat \ntrough steering east across the northwest region will bring a dry \ncold front across the area on Wednesday. This frontal passage will \nreturn elevated wind breezes, mainly over the southwest ID side.\nA large Pacific high pressure will then build in Thursday through\nFriday, brining unseasonably warm temperatures about 10 degrees\nabove normal for both those days. Come late Friday, another mostly\ndry shortwave trough will dig across the northwest region, \nreturning a cooling trend through Saturday. Sunday may see the \nreturn of warmer than normal temperatures, depending on the \nextent of Pacific ridge building over the Great Basin.",
